[prb@chinet.chi.il.us (Paul Botts) writes:]
[] A couple of questions from a new player:

okay being a novice and all ... the only way you'll get advice here
again is if this is the best game of your life ...

[] 1) Once you put a leash on your pet, how do you get it off?

_normally_ just re-apply it.  ever noticed that some weapons weld
themselves to your hand or that you can't remove some armor or rings?

[] 2) How do you convert an altar to your alignment?

SPOILER ALERT  {... discussion concerning altars and alignment ...}


assuming you're worthy (which is the norm after awhile) you simply
sacrifice (#offer) a corpse at the altar and if things are okay
the altar will convert to your alignment.  if this doesn't work
then things will get (perhaps insignificantly) bad for awhile ...
but should be able to wait it off.

[] 3) How do you change your own alignment?

the helm of opposite alignment works (for neutrals, persistence
allows you to choose lawful or chaotic).

if your god is angry at you and you sacrifice on a not co-aligned
altar then the chances are good that you'll be converted to the
alignment of the altar.  this is tricky to gauge.

if you sacrifice a unicorn of your alignment at a not co-aligned
altar you will change to the alignment of the altar.

changing alignment in this manner has its (temporary) drawbacks.

[] 4) Is there any way to escape a bear trap if you don't have
[] teleportation or levitation capability? I thought a wand of opening
[] might do it, but no go.

just keep struggling to get free and eventually you'll escape.
this isn't usually too much of a problem since you can still fight
while in the trap.

okay! don't come back until this is your best game ever ...

